  "caption": "Quinn lost three rounds to one jacket and can no longer reach the biscuits on the top shelf. Is it a frozen shoulder or a rotator cuff problem?\n\nA simple clue: if someone else can move your arm further than you can, it's often a cuff load issue. If it's stuck both ways, a stiff joint capsule is more likely.\n\nThe label matters: a hands-on movement check comes first. Stiff shoulders usually prefer gentle movement within comfort over forceful stretching, while cuff problems often respond to steady strengthening over 8 to 12 weeks. Patience is part of the plan.\n\nArm numbness, sudden weakness or pain after a fall is worth getting checked. If you have diabetes, check in earlier.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
